; with p−q>... 4p−3q>2; if p=q: p>2 (impossible), so pass better whenever correlation symmetric; need strong asymmetric. With near-identical copies, pass.\n\nCommand: pass.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"This is a twin prisoner's dilemma. EDT: sending gives (0 if quiet, 4 if letter); passing gives (2, 5). Correlation between copies. Need P(other sends | I send) = p, P(other sends | I pass) = q. Copies of same model with same reasoning — correlation high. Compute: V(send) = p·4 + (1-p)·0 = 4p. V(pass) = q·5 + (1-q)·2 = 2 + 3q. Send better iff 4p > 2+3q, i.e., 4p - 3q > 2. With high correlation p≈1, q≈0: V(send)=4 > 2. Cooperate-defect: defecting = send. Since copies are near-identical, sending → other sends, V(send)≈4? Wait: if both send, I get 4. If both pass, I get 2. Hmm, passing together is better (2 < 4). So EDT with perfect correlation: V(pass) = 2, V(send) = 4. Pass is better!\n\nRecheck: mutual pass = 2 years each; mutual send = 4 years each. EDT with twin correlation: pass gives 2, send gives 4. So keep quiet — EDT cooperates (pass = cooperate here, keeping quiet).\n\nEven with imperfect correlation: pass better iff 2+3q < 4p; with p−q>... 4p−3q>2; if p=q: p>2 (impossible), so pass better whenever correlation symmetric; need strong asymmetric. With near-identical copies, pass.\n\nCommand: pass.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":5626,"completion_tokens":543,"total_tokens":6169,"cost":0.00106164,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":448,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.00106164,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.00079014,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0002715},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":359,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}